Endpoint
- POST /responses (operationId: createResponse; tag: Responses)
- Summary: Create a model response
- Request body: application/json

Core request fields and constraints
- metadata: up to 16 key-value pairs
  - Keys: strings, max length 64
  - Values: strings, max length 512
- top_logprobs: integer 0–20 (returns up to N most likely tokens and their log probabilities)
- temperature: number 0–2 (default 1). Higher = more random; lower = more deterministic. Adjust temperature or top_p, not both.
- top_p: number 0–1 (default 1). Nucleus sampling; e.g., 0.1 = top 10% probability mass. Adjust top_p or temperature, not both.
- user: string (deprecated). Use safety_identifier and prompt_cache_key instead to keep caching benefits and safety best practices.
- safety_identifier: string. Stable hashed user identifier to help detect policy violations.
- prompt_cache_key: string. Stable identifier to improve prompt caching hit rates.
- service_tier: string enum with default auto
  - Values: auto, default, flex, scale, priority
  - Behavior:
    - auto uses project setting (defaults to default)
    - default = standard pricing/perf
    - flex or priority use the corresponding service tier
    - Response includes the actual service_tier used, which may differ from requested
- prompt_cache_retention: in-memory or 24h
  - 24h enables extended prompt caching (up to 24 hours)

Conversation and model selection
- previous_response_id: string or null. ID of a previous model response to create multi-turn conversations. Cannot be used with conversation.
- model: string; accepted values include many GPT/o-series variants
