General
- Base URL (proxy server): https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
- Endpoint: POST /chat/completions
- Purpose: Create a model response for a given chat conversation.

Request Body (application/json)
- messages (required, array, min 1): Conversation so far. Each item is one of:
  - System message:
    - role: "system" (required)
    - content: string (required)
    - name: string (optional)
  - User message:
    - role: "user" (required)
    - content (required):
      - string (text), or
      - array of content parts (min 1), each:
        - Text part: { type: "text", text: string }
        - Image part: { type: "image_url", image_url: { url: string (URL or base64), detail: "auto"|"low"|"high" (default "auto") } }
      - Image input supported when using gpt-4-vision-preview.
    - name: string (optional)
  - Assistant message:
    - role: "assistant" (required)
    - content: string | null (required unless tool_calls or function_call specified)
    - name: string (optional)
    - tool_calls: array of tool call objects (each required: id, type="function", function: { name: string, arguments: string (JSON; validate in your code) })
    - function_call (deprecated): { name: string, arguments: string (JSON; validate) }
  - Tool message:
    - role: "tool" (required)
    - content: string (required)
    - tool_call_id: string (required) — ID of the tool call being responded to
  - Function message (deprecated):
    - role: "function" (required)
    - content: string | null (required)
    - name: string (required)

- model (required): ID of model to use (string). Example: gpt-4-turbo. Enumerated options include:
  - gpt-4-turbo, gpt-4-turbo-2024-04-09
  - gpt-4-0125-preview, gpt-4-turbo-preview, gpt-4-1106-preview
  - gpt-4-vision-preview
  - gpt-4, gpt-4-0314, gpt-4-0613
  - gpt-4-32k, gpt-4-32k-0314, gpt-4-32k-0613
  - gpt-3.5-turbo, gpt-3.5-turbo-16k
  - gpt-3.5-turbo-0301, gpt-3.5-turbo-0613, gpt-3.5-turbo-1106, gpt-3.5-turbo-0125, gpt-3.5-turbo-16k-0613

Generation and sampling parameters
- max_tokens: integer | null. Max tokens generated. Total input + output limited by model context length.
- temperature: number [0,2], default 1. Higher = more random. Adjust either temperature or top_p, not both.
- top_p: number [0,1], default 1. Nucleus sampling; e.g., 0.1 = top 10% mass. Use instead of temperature (not both).
- n: integer [1,128], default 1. Number of choices to generate; costs scale with tokens across choices.
- stop: string | array of strings (1–4). Sequences where generation stops.
- frequency_penalty: number [-2,2], default 0. Positive reduces repetition based on token frequency.
- presence_penalty: number [-2,2], default 0. Positive encourages new topics.

Log probabilities
- logprobs: boolean | null, default false. If true, return logprobs for tokens in message content.
- top_logprobs: integer [0,20] | null. Number of most likely tokens at each position. Requires logprobs=true.

Token biasing
- logit_bias: map<number,int> | null. Map token IDs to bias [-100,100]. Bias added to logits; -100/100 can ban/exclusively select tokens.

Streaming
- stream: boolean | null, default false. If true, sends partial deltas via SSE; stream ends with data: [DONE].

Response formatting
- response_format: { type: "text" | "json_object" }, default "text".
  - JSON mode (type="json_object") guarantees valid JSON output.
  - Important: You must instruct the model to produce JSON in your prompts; otherwise it may emit whitespace until token limit. Content may be cut off if finish_reason="length".

Determinism (Beta)
- seed: integer | null (approx 64-bit signed range). Attempts deterministic sampling for same seed+params. Not guaranteed; monitor via system_fingerprint.

Tools and function calling
- tools: array of tool specs (max 128). Currently only functions supported:
  - Each tool: { type: "function", function: { name: string (A–Z, a–z, 0–9, underscores, dashes; max 64), descriptio
