General
- OpenAPI version: 3.1.0
- Title: OpenAI API; Description: REST API; Docs: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference
- Terms: https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use
- Contact: OpenAI Support (https://help.openai.com/)
- License: MIT (https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi/blob/master/LICENSE)
- Server: https://api.openai.com/v1
- Security: ApiKeyAuth (use Authorization: Bearer <token>)

Certificates API (Administration)
Endpoint: GET /organization/certificates (List organization certificates)
- Purpose: List uploaded certificates for the organization.
- Query parameters:
  - limit (integer, default 20, min 1, max 100): number of objects to return.
  - after (string): cursor-based pagination; pass the last object ID from a previous page.
  - order (string, enum asc|desc, default desc): sort by created_at.
- 200 Response (application/json):
  - object: "list"
  - data: array of certificate objects (see “Certificate object” below; during list they appear as "organization.certificate").
  - first_id: string
  - last_id: string
  - has_more: boolean
- Notes:
  - Use Bearer $OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY for org-level calls.
  - Example response shows items with object="organization.certificate", active=true, created_at, and certificate_details.valid_at/expires_at.

Endpoint: POST /organization/certificates (Upload certificate)
- Purpose: Upload a certificate to the organization. This does not automatically activate the certificate.
- Request body (application/json):
  - name (string, optional): friendly name.
  - content (string, required): certificate PEM content.
- 200 Response: a single certificate object (object="certificate"; see below).
- Limits: Organizations can upload up to 50 certificates.
- Example (abbreviated): POST with Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY and JSON including a name and PEM content; response returns object="certificate", id, name, created_at, certificate_details.valid_at/expires_at.

Certificate object
- Represents an individual certificate uploaded to the org (and appears with different object types depending on context/scope).
- Properties:
  - object (string, enum):
    - "certificate": for create/update/get a specific certificate.
    - "organization.certificate": when listing/activating/deactivating at organization scope.
    - "organization.project.certificate": when listing/activating/deactivating at project scope.
  - id (string): identifier used in API endpoints.
  - name (string): certificate name.
  - created_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when uploaded.
  - certificate_details (object):
    - valid_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when cert becomes valid.
    - expires_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when cert expires.
    - content (string): PEM content of the certificate.
  - active (boolean): whether the certificate is currently active at the given scope. Not returned when fetching a specific certificate.
- Required: object, id, name, created_at, certificate_details.

Example snippets (described)
- GET list: curl https://api.openai.com/v1/organization/certificates with Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY; response is a list with data entries like:
  - object="organization.certificate", id, name, active, created_at, certificate_details.valid_at/expires_at; plus first_id, last_id, has_more=false.
- POST upload: curl -X POST to /organization/certificates with Authorization and Content-Type: application/json; body includes name and PEM content; response returns object="certificate", id, name, created_at, certificate_details.valid_at/expires_at.

