Endpoint: GET /organization/users
- Summary: List users
- OperationId: list-users
- Tag: Users
- Description: Lists all users in the organization.
- Query parameters:
  - limit (integer, optional): 1–100, default 20
  - after (string, optional): Cursor for pagination; pass the last received ID to fetch next page
  - emails (array of string, optional): Filter users by email addresses
- 200 Response (application/json):
  - Schema (list object):
    - object: "list"
    - data: array of user objects
      - User object (organization.user):
        - object: "organization.user" (constant)
        - id (string): Identifier of the user
        - name (string)
        - email (string)
        - role (string enum): owner | reader
        - added_at (integer): Unix timestamp (seconds) when user was added
      - Required user fields: object, id, name, email, role, added_at
    - first_id (string)
    - last_id (string)
    - has_more (boolean)
    - Required list fields: object, data, first_id, last_id, has_more
  - Example response:
    {
      "object": "list",
      "data": [
        {
          "object": "organization.user",
          "id": "user_abc",
          "name": "First Last",
          "email": "user@example.com",
          "role": "owner",
          "added_at": 1711471533
        }
      ],
      "first_id": "user-abc",
      "last_id": "user-xyz",
      "has_more": false
    }
- Example request (curl):
  curl https://api.openai.com/v1/organization/users?after=user_abc&limit=20 \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_ADMIN_KEY" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json"
