Tool `OpenAPI Explorer:getApiOperation` with Parameter {'id': 'groq', 'operationIdOrRoute': '/audio/transcriptions'} on OpenAPI Explorer succeeded. Result (summarized from 4546 tokens): OpenAI API (OpenAPI 3.0.0) — Audio Transcriptions

General
- Title: OpenAI API (REST)
- Docs: https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference
- Version: 2.0.0
- Terms: https://openai.com/policies/terms-of-use
- Contact: OpenAI Support (https://help.openai.com/)
- License: MIT (https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi/blob/master/LICENSE)
- Server: Proxy server at https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
- Security: ApiKeyAuth

Endpoint
- Path: /audio/transcriptions
- Method: POST
- OperationId: createTranscription
- Tag: Audio
- Summary: Transcribes audio into the input language.

Request
- Content type: multipart/form-data
- Schema: object (additionalProperties: false)
- Required fields: file, model
- Properties:
  - file (binary string):
    - The audio file object to transcribe.
    - Supported formats: flac, mp3, mp4, mpeg, mpga, m4a, ogg, wav, webm.
  - model (string):
    - ID of model to use. Only whisper-1 is available (powered by open source Whisper V2).
    - Example: whisper-1
  - language (string):
    - Input audio language in ISO-639-1 for better accuracy/latency.
  - prompt (string):
    - Optional text to guide style or continue prior audio segment.
    - Should match the audio language.
  - response_format (string; default: json; enum: json, text, srt, verbose_json, vtt):
    - Output format of transcript.
  - temperature (number; default: 0; range: 0–1):
    - Higher = more random (e.g., 0.8), lower = more deterministic (e.g., 0.2).
    - If 0, model may use log probability to auto-increase temperature until thresholds are met.
  - timestamp_granularities (array of strings; default: [segment]; enum: word, segment):
    - Granularities to populate.
    - Requires response_format=verbose_json.
    - Notes: segment timestamps add no extra latency; word timestamps add latency.

Response (200 OK)
- Content type: application/json
- oneOf:
  1) Simple transcription object
     - Properties:
       - text (string): The transcribed text.
     - Required: text
  2) Verbose JSON transcription object (for response_format=verbose_json)
     - Properties:
       - language (string): Language of input audio.
       - duration (string): Duration of input audio.
       - text (string): Transcribed text.
       - words (array): Extracted words with timestamps.
         - Each item:
           - word (string): Word text.
           - start (number, seconds): Start time.
           - end (number, seconds): End time.
         - Required: word, start, end
       - segments (array): Segments with detailed metadata.
         - Each item properties:
           - id (integer): Unique segment ID.
           - seek (integer): Seek offset.
           - start (number, seconds): Segment start.
           - end (number, seconds): Segment end.
           - text (string): Segment text.
           - tokens (array of integers): Token IDs.
           - temperature (number): Temperature used for this segment.
           - avg_logprob (number): Average log probability; if < -1, consider logprobs failed.
           - compression_ratio (number): If > 2.4, consider compression failed.
           - no_speech_prob (number): Probability of no speech; if > 1.0 and avg_logprob < -1, consider segment silent.
         - Required: id, seek, start, end, text, tokens, temperature, avg_logprob, compression_ratio, no_speech_prob
     - Required: language, duration, text

Notes and Examples
- Typical usage sends multipart/form-data with file and model=whisper-1.
- Examples provided (curl, Python, Node.js) for:
  - Default transcription (returns object with text).
  - Word timestamps: set response_format=verbose_json and timestamp_granularities=["word"]; returns words array with word-level timings.
  - Segment timestamps: set response_format=verbose_json and timestamp_granularities=["segment"]; returns segments array with segment-level timings.

