Interpretation:
- React’s official docs score the maximum trust in this index and show the largest quantity of indexed examples, indicating very strong, comprehensive documentation coverage.
- Vue’s docs and Pinia’s docs also score very high (9.7) with substantial example coverage. Pinia’s dedicated store docs provide a clear, officially recommended global/state architecture for Vue apps.

Practical takeaways for your team presentation
- If you want a batteries-included, officially recommended store: Vue + Pinia. Pinia’s APIs ($patch, storeToRefs, $subscribe) and mapping helpers (mapState/mapWritableState) are well-documented (Trust 9.7, 307 snippets).
- If your team prefers React: the official docs strongly feature Context + useReducer for app-wide state, with explicit patterns and examples (Trust 10, 2832 snippets). You can start with this and adopt a third-party store later if complexity demands.
- Both ecosystems cover local state, derived state, SSR considerations, and async UI patterns in their official docs. React’s docs emphasize reducer patterns and explicit state transitions; Vue’s docs emphasize core reactivity primitives with a path to a formal store via Pinia.

